# DURABLE REPRO — D10 exclusivity hole A2: a `.get()`-chain element VIEW passed
# alongside an `&` writer of the SAME collection.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend, `gg build --sanitize`):
# `gg check` says "OK: no semantic errors" and the binary dies with
#   AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free ... in gorget_string_copy_cow
# The `.get(0).unwrap()` view is not a participant in `check_call_aliasing`
# (no MethodCall arm in `find_root_def_id_with_path`), so the writer `&v` is
# free to realloc the backing store out from under a live borrow of an element.
#
# INTENDED: REJECTED at `gg check` with `E_BorrowConflict` — the read and the
# writer name overlapping places, which is exactly the D10 "one exclusive
# writer" rule. (The byte-identical shape spelled `f(v[0], &v)` over a plain
# local ALREADY rejects; this is the same program in a costume the syntactic
# check does not recognize.)
#
# ⚠⚠ ORACLE NOTE FOR THE WHOLE `sound_excl_*` FAMILY — ggdef is NOT the
# authority here, and it is worth knowing why before anyone reaches for it.
# Measured this session: ggdef ACCEPTS every in-subset fixture of this family
# (`..._getchain_local`, `..._getchain_fieldpath`, `..._getchain_alias_
# provenance`, `..._receiver_writer`, `..._nested_writer_{call,closure,ctor,
# tuple,index_store}`, `..._forbody_amp_writer`) and prints the pre-mutation
# value cleanly. That is not a verdict that the programs are sound — ggdef is a
# definitional INTERPRETER with value semantics, so no reallocation can
# invalidate anything and the UAF is structurally unobservable in that lane.
# The intended REJECT comes from the ratified owner ruling on the D10
# exclusivity holes ("(b) STRUCTURAL … neg fixture per hole", 2026-07-22), and
# ggdef owes the same reject as part of that landing (Core #9).
# The remaining fixtures of the family are outside ggdef's phase-0 subset:
#   ..._getchain_static          -> "item kind static is outside the phase-0 subset"
#   ..._overload_alias_twin      -> "operator Add on struct and struct"
#   ..._match_scrutinee_...      -> "method `.first()` is outside the phase-0 subset"
# Contrast the `sound_amp_owning_position_*` class, where ggdef DOES reject and
# IS the oracle.
#
# The 4096-push loop FORCES a real reallocation — a smaller/constant-capacity
# shape is a false negative.
#
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High): the D10 "one exclusive writer"
# structural-chokepoint entry, hole #1.
void f(String s, Vector[String] &v):
    int i = 0
    while i < 4096:
        v.push("filler-padding-to-force-a-real-reallocation")
        i = i + 1
    print(s)

void main():
    Vector[String] v = Vector[String]()
    v.push("alpha-heap-forced-payload")
    f(v.get(0).unwrap(), &v)
